WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.582 --> 00:00:16.464
Jason hadn't put down his video game all day.

2
00:00:17.344 --> 00:00:21.006
He was too busy trying to reach level five of Dragon Lands.

3
00:00:21.927 --> 00:00:25.409
Right now he was battling dragons on the way to Kids Central.

4
00:00:26.409 --> 00:00:30.852
He was about to reach the final battle of level four when Smack!

5
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.121
He walked right into Nina.

6
00:00:33.141 --> 00:00:35.082
"Watch where you're going!"

7
00:00:35.522 --> 00:00:36.123
she cried.

8
00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:42.907
Nina. I'm trying to finish—" he began.

9
00:00:42.927 --> 00:00:48.350
"It's time to put the video game away," Miss Shelly reminded Jason.

10
00:00:49.271 --> 00:00:53.913
"For today's activity, you'll need a book.

11
00:00:54.874 --> 00:00:56.115
Grab a dictionary!"

12
00:00:57.035 --> 00:00:57.916
Bobby groaned.

13
00:00:59.044 --> 00:01:00.785
"A dictionary?

14
00:01:01.165 --> 00:01:06.128
Why?" Miss Shelly held up a thick piece of paper with her name on it.

15
00:01:06.989 --> 00:01:09.370
"We're making name poem bookmarks."

16
00:01:10.491 --> 00:01:12.892
Jason tucked his game into his backpack.

17
00:01:12.912 --> 00:01:14.953
"What's a name poem?"

18
00:01:14.973 --> 00:01:20.516
"It's a poem that uses the letters in your name," Miss Shelly explained.

19
00:01:20.536 --> 00:01:22.978
"My first name is Marie.

20
00:01:23.578 --> 00:01:26.500
So the first word in my poem will begin with M.

21
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.381
The next line will begin with A.

22
00:01:30.242 --> 00:01:31.963
Every line should describe you."

23
00:01:36.407 --> 00:01:37.127
Ethan said.

24
00:01:37.147 --> 00:01:39.049
"What's that, Ethan?"

25
00:01:39.449 --> 00:01:40.450
Miss Shelly asked.

26
00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:44.052
"That could be the first word in your poem," he said.

27
00:01:44.072 --> 00:01:46.994
"Because like magic, you make things fun."

28
00:01:47.014 --> 00:01:50.057
"What are the dictionaries for?"

29
00:01:50.457 --> 00:01:51.177
asked Nina.

30
00:01:51.197 --> 00:01:54.460
"Dictionaries help when you can't think of a word."

31
00:01:55.432 --> 00:01:57.613
Miss Shelly handed out blank bookmarks.

32
00:01:59.214 --> 00:02:01.335
"Write your name poem on these when you're done.

33
00:02:01.996 --> 00:02:03.837
Then you can use them as bookmarks."

34
00:02:05.338 --> 00:02:07.799
Jason scribbled his name on a piece of paper.

35
00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:11.421
J wasn't the easiest letter to start with.

36
00:02:11.441 --> 00:02:13.742
"Jolly?" he thought.

37
00:02:13.762 --> 00:02:17.424
"Sounds too much like Santa Claus."

38
00:02:18.485 --> 00:02:19.525
Next was A.

39
00:02:20.346 --> 00:02:21.126
He sighed.

40
00:02:22.087 --> 00:02:23.848
He was awful at writing poems.

41
00:02:24.852 --> 00:02:29.136
"Awful! 'Awful' begins with A!"

42
00:02:30.237 --> 00:02:32.199
He stared at the S and yawned.

43
00:02:32.219 --> 00:02:36.102
"Sleepy!" he thought.

44
00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:37.663
That was easy.

45
00:02:38.604 --> 00:02:39.525
Then there was O.

46
00:02:40.486 --> 00:02:43.688
Jason opened the dictionary to the first page of Oo.

47
00:02:44.649 --> 00:02:49.133
There were mostly words he didn't know, like "obsolete" and "obscure."

48
00:02:50.054 --> 00:02:52.016
He looked through all the letter O words.

49
00:02:53.376 --> 00:02:57.039
He decided that "odd" was the only O word that might work.

50
00:02:58.941 --> 00:03:03.204
When everyone was finished, Miss Shelly called on Ethan to read his poem.

51
00:03:03.224 --> 00:03:09.770
"Excellent surfer, Totally cool, Helpful, Adventurous, and New," he read.

52
00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.412
"Because I'm still new to Sunny Dale."

53
00:03:14.674 --> 00:03:15.795
Jason was next.

54
00:03:15.815 --> 00:03:20.459
"Jumpy, Awful, Sleepy, Odd, Nut," he read.

55
00:03:20.479 --> 00:03:23.693
"Nut?" Izzie asked, confused.

56
00:03:23.713 --> 00:03:28.017
"I saw that 'nut' can mean a strange or silly person," he said.

57
00:03:28.037 --> 00:03:32.821
"Jason, are you sure those words describe you?"

58
00:03:33.301 --> 00:03:34.282
Miss Shelly asked.

59
00:03:34.883 --> 00:03:38.766
"They're not bad words, but I could think of nicer words."

60
00:03:39.927 --> 00:03:43.530
"Yeah, like J for 'Jigsaw puzzle wizard!'"

61
00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:44.530
Bobby said.

62
00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:46.752
"You're great at puzzles."

63
00:03:46.772 --> 00:03:51.156
"And A for 'awesome,'" Nina said.

64
00:03:52.124 --> 00:03:54.086
"S for 'super,'" Izzie added.

65
00:03:54.106 --> 00:03:55.427
"Or 'sweet.'"

66
00:03:55.447 --> 00:04:01.092
"O for the 'only' person who can reach level four in the Dragon Lands video game!"

67
00:04:01.493 --> 00:04:02.213
Ethan said.

68
00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:04.576
Jason smiled.

69
00:04:04.596 --> 00:04:06.517
"You guys are good at this!"

70
00:04:07.578 --> 00:04:09.420
He began writing his new poem.

71
00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:13.724
"But keep N for 'nut,'" Bobby said, grinning.

72
00:04:13.744 --> 00:04:16.987
"Because you can be pretty strange."
